# Directory architecture

```
src/
  main.ts             # bootstrap only: Nest factory, Swagger, listen
  app.module.ts       # root module: ConfigModule + feature modules
  app.setup.ts        # configureApp(): global pipes, reused by main.ts AND e2e tests
  config/             # env validation (Joi schema) + its spec
  prisma/             # PrismaModule / PrismaService (global provider)
  modules/<feature>/  # one folder per feature module
  shared/             # code used by 2+ modules
test/                 # *.e2e-spec.ts, setup-env.ts, shared test helpers
prisma/               # schema.prisma + migrations
```

## Feature module layout

Everything a feature owns stays inside `src/modules/<feature>/`:

```
modules/auth/
  auth.module.ts        # wiring, providers, exports
  auth.controller.ts    # HTTP surface + Swagger decorators
  auth.service.ts       # business logic
  auth.constants.ts     # TTLs, limits — no magic numbers in services
  dto/                  # request/response shapes with class-validator
  guards/               # route guards
```

File names are `<name>.<role>.ts` (`auth-cookies.service.ts`, `session-auth.guard.ts`, `public-user.dto.ts`). Never reach into another module's internals — import only what its module `exports`.

## Shared code

When the same logic is needed by a **second** module, move it to `src/shared/` and import it from both. Do not copy-paste, and do not pre-create a shared helper for a single caller (see ponytail: YAGNI).

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — same normalization pasted in two modules
// modules/auth/dto/register.dto.ts AND modules/chat/dto/create-chat.dto.ts
@Transform(({ value }) => typeof value === 'string' ? value.trim().toLowerCase() : value)

// ✅ GOOD — one home, both import it
// src/shared/normalize.ts
export const normalizeEmail = ({ value }: TransformFnParams) =>
  typeof value === 'string' ? value.trim().toLowerCase() : value;
```

Test-only helpers duplicated across e2e specs belong in a `test/` helper file, not `src/shared` — `src/` ships to `dist/`.
